luation","slug":"monitoring_and_evaluation","type":"overview","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64372":{"name":"Co-benefits","slug":"cobenefits","type":"overview","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64373":{"name":"International Frameworks","slug":"international_frameworks","type":"overview","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64374":{"name":"Gender and Indigenous People","slug":"gender_and_indigenous_people","type":"overview","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64375":{"name":"Loss and Damage","slug":"loss_and_damage","type":"overview","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64376":{"name":"Loss and Damage","slug":"loss_and_damage","type":"map","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64377":{"name":"Transformative Adaptation","slug":"transformative_adaptation","type":"overview","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64378":{"name":"Transformative Adaptation","slug":"transformative_adaptation","type":"map","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64379":{"name":"Children and Young People","slug":"children_and_young_people","type":"overview","sources":["UNICEF"]},"64380":{"name":"Vulnerability","slug":"vulnerability","type":"overview","sources":["UNICEF","NDC Explorer"]},"64381":{"name":"Climate Risks","slug":"climate_risks","type":"overview","sources":["NDC Explorer"]},"64382":{"name":"Mitigation: GHG Target Type","slug":"mitigation_ghg_target_type","type":"map","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64383":{"name":"Mitigation: Sector Coverage","slug":"mitigation_sector_coverage","type":"map","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64384":{"name":"Mitigation: Gas Coverage","slug":"mitigation_gas_coverage","type":"map","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64385":{"name":"Fairness, Ambition and Objective","slug":"fairness_ambition_and_objective","type":"overview","sources":["Climate Watch"]}},"sectors":{},"indicators":[{"id":648348,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"NDC summary","slug":"indc_summary","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64321,64324],"labels":{},"locations":{"MAR":[{"value":"Please note that the NDC was submitted only in French. WRI did its best to translate the NDC language. If any errors are identified, please contact us at ClimateWatch@WRI.org.\u003cbr\u003e\"An unconditional net reduction in GHG emissions across the economy of 21.6% in 2035 compared to the baseline scenario (Normal Business Course), with the country's own resources, and secure international support to date. A conditional net reduction in economy-wide GHG emissions of 31.4% in 2035 compared to the Reference Case (Normal Business Course), thus raising the national ambition to reduce GHG emissions to 53% in 2035 compared to the Reference Case (NAC).\"","document_slug":"third_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Morocco commits to reduce GHG emissions by 18.3% (unconditional) and 45.5% (conditional) in 2030, compared to the BAU scenario.\u003cbr\u003eThe submission also has an adaptation part.","document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Morocco\u0026rsquo;s commitment is to reduce its GHG emissions by 32% by 2030 compared to business as usual\" projected emissions. This commitment is contingent upon gaining access to new sources of finance and enhanced support, compared to that received over the past years, within the context of a new legally-binding agreement under the auspices of the UNFCCC. This target translates into a cumulative reduction of 401 Mt CO\u003csub\u003e2\u003c/sub\u003eeq over the period 2020\u0026shy;-2030. Meeting this target will require an overall investment in the order of USD 45 billion, of which USD 35 billion is conditional upon international support through new climate finance mechanisms, such as the Green Climate Fund.\"\u003cbr /\u003eMorocco\u0026rsquo;s mitigation target is divided into a conditional and unconditional target: The unconditional target is a 13% reduction in GHG emissions by 2030 compared to a business as usual (BAU) scenario, while the conditional target is an additional 19% reduction achievable under certain conditions, which would bring the total GHG reduction to 32% below BAU emission levels by 2030. Note: Morocco reserves the right to revise said BAU scenario on the basis of new analysis by 2020.\u003cbr /\u003eMorocco has also submitted a section on adaptation, outlining its vision, goals, needs, and system for monitoring and evaluation.","document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Morocco\u0026rsquo;s commitment is to reduce its GHG emissions by 32% by 2030 compared to business as usual\" projected emissions. This commitment is contingent upon gaining access to new sources of finance and enhanced support, compared to that received over the past years, within the context of a new legally-binding agreement under the auspices of the UNFCCC. This target translates into a cumulative reduction of 401 Mt CO\u003csub\u003e2\u003c/sub\u003eeq over the period 2020\u0026shy;-2030. Meeting this target will require an overall investment in the order of USD 45 billion, of which USD 35 billion is conditional upon international support through new climate finance mechanisms, such as the Green Climate Fund.\"\u003cbr /\u003eMorocco\u0026rsquo;s mitigation target is divided into a conditional and unconditional target: The unconditional target is a 13% reduction in GHG emissions by 2030 compared to a business as usual (BAU) scenario, while the conditional target is an additional 19% reduction achievable under certain conditions, which would bring the total GHG reduction to 32% below BAU emission levels by 2030. Note: Morocco reserves the right to revise said BAU scenario on the basis of new analysis by 2020.\u003cbr /\u003eMorocco has also submitted a section on adaptation, outlining its vision, goals, needs, and system for monitoring and evaluation.","document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648353,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"GHG target","slug":"ghg_target","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64321,64326],"labels":{},"locations":{"MAR":[{"value":"Morocco commits to reducing its emissions by 21.6% by 2035 compared to BAU (unconditional). Morocco also commits to reducing its emissions by an additional 31.4% (53% reduction in total) by 2035 compared to BAU, conditional on international support.","document_slug":"third_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Reduce GHG emissions by 18.3% (unconditional) and 45.5% (conditional) in 2030, compared to the BAU scenario.","document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"32% reduction in GHG emission by 2030 compared to the BAU scenario, taking into account reductions in Agriculture, Forestry and Other Land Use (AFOLU)","document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"32% reduction in GHG emission by 2030 compared to the BAU scenario, taking into account reductions in Agriculture, Forestry and Other Land Use (AFOLU)","document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648356,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Target year (mitigation)","slug":"time_target_year","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64321,64324,64325],"labels":{"1283659":{"name":"2025","slug":null,"index":1},"1283660":{"name":"2030","slug":null,"index":2},"1283661":{"name":"2035","slug":null,"index":3},"1283662":{"name":"2040","slug":null,"index":4},"1283663":{"name":"2025 and 2030","slug":null,"index":5},"1283664":{"name":"2030 and 2035","slug":null,"index":6},"1283665":{"name":"Other","slug":null,"index":7},"1283666":{"name":"Not Applicable","slug":null,"index":8},"1283667":{"name":"No Document Submitted","slug":null,"index":-2}},"locations":{"MAR":[{"value":"2035","label_id":1283661,"document_slug":"third_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"2030","label_id":1283660,"document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"2030","label_id":1283660,"document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"2030","label_id":1283660,"document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648361,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Conditionality","slug":"conditionality","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64321,64324,64328],"labe